| `test_quality.assertions.helper_depth` | integer | `3` in keel and in a generated project; absent, the same value, which its reader reports as `[using default] test_quality.assertions.helper_depth = 3` | a whole number, 1 or more | `tests/assertion_quality.py` (`policy`, `scan`), called by `tests/integration/test_assertion_quality_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `test_quality.assertions.helper_depth` row | Sets how many calls below a test the assertion-quality gate follows to find an assertion in a helper: 1 follows only the helpers the test calls itself. A test whose only assertion sits deeper fails as having no assertion. Keel's own suite needs 1; the gate reads the same findings at 1, 2, 3 and 6. A cycle of helpers is followed once round, whatever the depth. A value below 1 or not an integer (including a boolean) fails the gate with `SourceTreeError`, preserving the loader's diagnostic lines and naming this key. | a cap on the gate's run time: its parsed-module cache holds at most `tests.cache_max_entries` entries and may reparse evicted modules | always |
